-- title:
--   §3, PART 1, p. 9 — $\widetilde S_{\bar{\mathcal I}}\subseteq S_{\bar{\mathcal I}}$ up to a probability 0 set
-- statement:
--   Let $(\Delta,\mathcal D,\mathbb P)$ be a probability space, $c\in\mathbb R^d$, $\mathcal X$ and $\mathcal X_\delta$ ($\delta\in\Delta$) subsets of $\mathbb R^d$, and suppose that every program $P_k$ (minimise $c^\top x$ over $\mathcal X\cap\bigcap_{i\le k}\mathcal X_{\delta^{(i)}}$) has a unique solution $x^*_k$. Assume the problem is **fully-supported** (Definition 2.3): for every $m\ge d$, with $\mathbb P^m$-probability one the program $P_m$ has exactly $d$ support constraints. Then, for every $m\ge d$,
--   $$\mathbb P^m\big(\widetilde S_{\bar{\mathcal I}}\setminus S_{\bar{\mathcal I}}\big)=0,$$
--   where $\widetilde S_{\bar{\mathcal I}}$ is the set where $\delta^{(d+1)},\dots,\delta^{(m)}$ are not violated by the solution generated by $\delta^{(1)},\dots,\delta^{(d)}$, and $S_{\bar{\mathcal I}}$ is the set where the support constraints are exactly $\delta^{(1)},\dots,\delta^{(d)}$.
--
--   Together with $S_{\bar{\mathcal I}}\subseteq\widetilde S_{\bar{\mathcal I}}$ this gives $\mathbb P^m\{S_{\bar{\mathcal I}}\}=\mathbb P^m\{\widetilde S_{\bar{\mathcal I}}\}$, the identity on which the computation of (3.3) rests.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** "Up to a probability 0 set" is stated as: the $\mathbb P^m$-(outer) measure of $\widetilde S_{\bar{\mathcal I}}\setminus S_{\bar{\mathcal I}}$ is zero. Full support is the published `FullySupported` (almost sure, not pointwise; footnote 3, p. 7). Existence and uniqueness are assumed for every number of constraints, with the solution family `θs`. Convexity, closedness and measurability are not needed and not assumed. Indexes are 0-based.
-- source:
--   Campi & Garatti, The exact feasibility of randomized solutions of uncertain convex programs, SIAM J. Optim. 19(3) (2008); authors' final manuscript, p. 9, 'S̃_𝓘̄ ⊆ S_𝓘̄ up to a probability 0 set'

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ScenarioApproach_Generalization_violation
import Definitions.Def_ScenarioApproach_Generalization_scenarioProgram
import Definitions.Def_ScenarioApproach_Generalization_supportConstraint
import Definitions.Def_ScenarioExact_PartOne_Basic
open MeasureTheory ScenarioApproach.Generalization
open scoped ENNReal

namespace ScenarioExact.PartOne

/-- §3, PART 1, p. 9: `S̃_𝓘̄ ⊆ S_𝓘̄` up to a probability 0 set. For a fully-supported
problem and `m ≥ d`, the multi-extractions in `S̃_𝓘̄` but not in `S_𝓘̄` form a `ℙ^m`-null set. -/
theorem Stilde_subset_ae {d m : ℕ} {Δ : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Δ]
    (P : Measure Δ) [IsProbabilityMeasure P]
    (c : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)) (Θ : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)))
    (Θδ : Δ → Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)))
    (hexu : ∀ (k : ℕ) (ω : Fin k → Δ), ∃! θ, IsSolution c Θ Θδ ω θ)
    (θs : (k : ℕ) → (Fin k → Δ) → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d))
    (hθs : ∀ (k : ℕ) (ω : Fin k → Δ), IsSolution c Θ Θδ ω (θs k ω))
    (hfs : FullySupported c Θ Θδ P)
    (hm : d ≤ m) :
    Measure.pi (fun _ : Fin m => P) (Stilde Θδ θs hm \ S c Θ Θδ θs (Ibar d m)) = 0 := by sorry

end ScenarioExact.PartOne
